    "review_findings": [
      "All 31 fixed-scope paths exist and match their exact recorded SHA-256. The frozen research trio, canonical configuration and extension draft match the reviewed scope.",
      "The eight Mercy Killer formal pages and related map, both reverse weapon pages, blessing catalogs and glossary consistently identify two variants and four bindings: Catachan Combat Blade Mk III/Mk VI and Improvised Shivs Mk I/Mk III. Trait/item restrictions, RAW keys, per-variant pages and icon identity agree.",
      "Both own I–IV tiers are .525/.55/.575/.6 with the expected percentage formatter. The actual wrappers clone the bleeding base template; the held-slot conditional fallback 1.0 is replaced by the own conditional value rather than added.",
      "The implementation gate is melee plus weakspot plus the target bleeding keyword already present at damage calculation; it does not scale with bleed-stack count. Attack damage calculation precedes post-hit buff handling, so a bleed applied by that same hit cannot retroactively qualify it. Bleed periodic damage is attack_type=buff and is excluded.",
      "The Combat Blade special jab is an actual melee sweep/punch and can qualify when its hit independently meets the gate. Both Shivs specials are ranged projectile throws; their wired neurotoxin applies toxin, not bleeding, so these special hits do not qualify.",
      "The controlled examples correctly use F*(S+t), with final damage B+F*(S+t) only when later multipliers are neutral: at B=200,F=100,S=1, baseline 300 and tier IV 360 (+20%); tier I is 352.5 and IV is +2.13% over I final damage. At S=1.4, baseline 340 and tier IV 400 (+17.65%). These are not claims that the tier multiplies the entire final hit.",
      "All four EN/ZH RAW tier sentences and static reconstructions preserve the source wording and values. The implementation-only conditions are identified as documentation coverage rather than a false RAW contradiction. The 128px icon path, id and verified attachment are kept distinct and consistent.",
      "The focused source receipt records 52 ranges across 22 source files; link and GFM checks report no new errors, and the current shared-map partition checks pass. These validations agree with the peer-reviewed pages and indexes."
    ],
